# Deliberate exceptions for tools/check-test-imports.sh — one path per line, with a reason.
#
# A file belongs here only when reading `DATABASE_URL` is the code's JOB: an operator
# supplied the variable and this is the code that honours it. Test code never qualifies
# — it must use `fraiseql_test_support::database_url()` (panics with an actionable
# message) or `try_database_url()` (the explicit self-skipping form), so that a CI leg
# which forgets to inject the URL fails loudly instead of silently retargeting a
# different database. That silent-default shape is what #1075 found behind a gate that
# could never fire.
#
# The gate fails on a stale row too, so an entry that stops reading the variable must
# be removed rather than left as an exemption nobody prunes.

# `fraiseql-cli` subcommands: DATABASE_URL is the documented fallback for the
# `--database-url` flag, so these are the code that implements the fallback.
crates/fraiseql-cli/src/commands/migrate.rs
crates/fraiseql-cli/src/commands/generate_views.rs
crates/fraiseql-cli/src/commands/doctor.rs
crates/fraiseql-cli/src/commands/query.rs
crates/fraiseql-cli/src/commands/run.rs

# The server's CLI config loader: DATABASE_URL is one of the documented sources the
# runtime config resolves from, ahead of the TOML value.
crates/fraiseql-server/src/cli.rs
